# cuts/v1.0.51/cut.env -- the pins this cut is made from.
#
# 🔴 WHY THIS FILE EXISTS, AND WHY IT WAS THE FIFTH THING MISSING.
# v1.0.51's preflight refused four separate times before this file was written:
# the installer version stamp, the OS003 BOM, the walk-closure row, and the cut
# manifest. This is the fifth input. It was found WITHOUT spending a fifth run,
# by enumerating all 17 preflight steps and executing the runnable ones locally
# -- which is what should have happened after the first refusal instead of the
# fourth. preflight stops at the first failing step, so each run reveals exactly
# one blocker and no more. Reading the whole step list costs one command.
#
# The two gates that name this file both spoke clearly when run locally:
#   scripts/verify_cut_pin_is_current.sh --cut v1.0.51 --ref HEAD
#       rc=2  CANNOT-RUN: no cuts/v1.0.51/cut.env
#   ./tests/test_rollforward_registry_pin.sh
#       rc=1  FAIL  cut-manifests/v1.0.51.yaml is the newest cut but
#             cuts/v1.0.51/cut.env does NOT exist -- 'rollforward_gate.sh
#             --cut v1.0.51' dies with PARSE ERROR, preflight goes red, and the
#             cut job is SKIPPED with nothing signed
# The second is the better message: it names the CONSEQUENCE, not just the
# mismatch. A CANNOT-RUN that also tells you what breaks downstream is worth
# more than a FAIL that only says "no".
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 🔴 DAEMON_COMMIT NAMES THE ARTEFACT, NOT THE TREE. DO NOT "UPDATE" IT.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Carried UNCHANGED from v1.0.50 at f1c7c57d, and it must not be advanced.
# THIS CUT REBUILDS NO DAEMON. Every one of the four fixes it carries is in
# install.sh, which is CM051's own file; nothing under crates/ or web/ is
# touched, so cut.env's own rule -- any path that reaches the artefact forces a
# rebuild -- is not triggered.
#
# If a later reader finds oa main ahead of this pin, the correct response is NOT
# to advance this line. It is to ask whether the daemon must be REBUILT. The
# artefact is the fact; the tree is the claim; when they disagree, change the
# claim. Editing this line to match a moved tree is how a cut acquires false
# provenance, which is the v1.0.14 failure.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CM051 -- WHY a8cfee86, AND WHY IT SURVIVES THIS FILE'S OWN MERGE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CM051 names the tree whose install.sh SHIPS, compared by BLOB IDENTITY and not
# by ancestry (verify_cut_pin_is_current.sh self-test 6).
#
# a8cfee86 is main after all three earlier v1.0.51 prerequisites landed: #1270
# (the version stamp, at the XcodeGen spec rather than its generated output),
# #1271 (the v1.0.50 walk-closure row) and #1272 (the vendored OS003 BOM).
#
# 🔴 THE TWO-PR RULE DOES NOT BIND HERE, AND THE REASON MATTERS. v1.0.46's
# header records that a pin and the WITNESS to that pin cannot ride the same
# commit -- because bundling them leaves CM051= naming a tree whose install.sh
# no longer exists on main. That hazard exists only when install.sh is MOVING.
# It is not moving here: the last commit to touch install.sh is c93e0f83
# (#1269), and everything after it -- #1270 gui/, #1271 cuts/, #1272 cuts/, and
# this PR's cut-manifests/ + cuts/ -- leaves the blob untouched. So the blob at
# a8cfee86 is the blob at the merge of this PR, and the pin stays true across
# its own landing. That is a MEASURED exemption, not a waiver.
#
# ⚠️ IT BECOMES BINDING THE MOMENT ANYTHING TOUCHES install.sh. If a further PR
# lands on install.sh before the tag, this pin is stale and re-running
# verify_cut_pin_is_current.sh is mandatory, not optional. v1.0.46's header says
# it plainly and it is repeated here because it already happened once: "a pin
# chosen early and trusted is a pin that goes stale while you are not looking".
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT THIS CUT CARRIES, AND WHAT IT DELIBERATELY DOES NOT
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CARRIES, all four in install.sh, each mutation-tested against its own pre-fix
# parent and each holding a row in cut-manifests/v1.0.51.yaml:
#   #1266  cm052 pip staged outside the notarised bundle  (board #422)
#   #1267  FDA listed-ness never synthesised from the nudge (board #571)
#   #1269  engine-supervisor plist roots at OSTLER_FINAL_DIR (board #573)
#          plus the store-port probe self-test that adjudicated its own red
#          as a pass
#
# DOES NOT CARRY, stated so the walk is not a surprise:
#   #547  identity_resolver spins at 100% CPU forever on an empty dataset and
#         is orphaned to PPID 1 after install.sh exits "successfully"
#   #543  the consent screen may tell the customer that declining public
#         look-ups stops Wikidata/MusicBrainz/OpenLibrary contact, while the
#         one-shot enrichment pass is not gated by that answer
#   #519  3 of 23 LaunchAgents are never loaded and install.sh reports success,
#         because `launchctl load` exits 0 on failure
#   #509  `launchctl kickstart -k` blocks on a penalty-boxed job, 5 call sites
# The freshness, grounding and usage-journal probes WILL therefore still fail
# this walk. That is expected and is not a reason to withhold the cut: the walk
# gates PROMOTION, not assembly.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 🔴 THIS CUT HAS NO WALK RECORD AT THE MOMENT IT IS MADE, AND THAT IS CORRECT.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# walks/v1.0.51.tsv does not exist, so verify_walk_record.sh returns rc=2 --
# absence, correctly not conflated with badness -- PROMOTE=0, the release is a
# prerelease, and ostler.ai/install.dmg keeps resolving to v1.0.41. The sequence
# is cut -> walk -> record -> only then promote. A green cut is not a shipped
# one, and nothing between "gates green" and "customer download" is a runtime
# proof until a walker runs it.
#
# ⚠️ BEFORE THE WALK, ONE PRECAUTION THAT COSTS NOTHING (TNM, 2026-08-29):
# put the DMG in the WALKED ACCOUNT'S ~/Downloads. post_walk_qa.sh looks in only
# three directories of the ssh user it walks as -- $HOME/Downloads, $HOME/Desktop
# and $HOME -- and on a CLEAN record the gate then REQUIRES
# artefact_sha256_source to read measured(...) and exits 2 otherwise. That
# CLEAN-scoped block has never executed in this project's history, because there
# has never been a clean record. A clean walk whose DMG sits elsewhere would
# produce PROMOTE=0 for a reason that reads as "no walk evidence" rather than
# "wrong folder", on the one run where everyone is tired and reading the verdict
# instead of the field.

CUT_VERSION=1.0.51
DAEMON_COMMIT=f1c7c57d
CM051=a8cfee86   # main after #1270 + #1271 + #1272. install.sh blob is unchanged
                 # since c93e0f83 (#1269), so this pin names the blob that ships
                 # and stays true across this file's own merge. Re-run
                 # scripts/verify_cut_pin_is_current.sh immediately before the
                 # tag push anyway -- that instruction is in this file because
                 # trusting an early pin has already cost a cut once.
